I am in the living room now.
There is a small sofa.
I call my mother in Mexico.
"Hi Mom," I say.
"Hi Maya," my mother says.
"Where are you?" she asks.
"I am in Copenhagen," I answer.
"I am in the apartment now."
"That is so good," my mother says.
"Is it big?" she asks.
"No, it is small," I answer.
"But it is cozy, and I am happy."
"Is it cold?" she asks.
"Yes, it is cold outside," I say.
"But it is warm in here."
"I am safe."
"That is good," my mother says.
I smile.
Denmark is my new home.
